load @term/seed/code/structure/field
  find field

load @term/seed/code/structure/set
  find set

load @term/seed/code/structure/function/binary
  find binary-function

# A Lie algebra: a vector space with a bracket that is antisymmetric (the bracket of a thing with itself is zero) and
# obeys the Jacobi identity (the bracket cyclically distributes over itself). The bracket is the infinitesimal commutator,
# what is left of a group's multiplication near its identity, so a Lie algebra is the linear shadow of a continuous
# symmetry. The rotations of the eight-dimensional arena form the simple Lie algebra of type D4, of rank four, and its
# roots are the twenty-four vertices of the 24-cell. The rank four is read as the four dimensions of spacetime, and the
# threefold symmetry of its diagram is triality. So the Lie algebra is where the geometry of the substrate turns into the
# symmetry the physics runs on.
form lie-algebra
  link field, like field
  link set, like set
  link bracket, like binary-function
